# Article: Pack (six)

Roles: specifier, coder, cleaner, architect, hardener, qa.

Chain: specifier -> coder -> cleaner -> architect -> hardener -> qa,
then qa broadcasts completion to every other role.

- specifier turns a request into an accepted specification, then sends a
  git_handoff to coder.
- coder implements the specified slice, then forwards to cleaner.
- cleaner cleans the implementation, then forwards to architect.
- architect reviews structure and boundaries, then forwards to hardener.
- hardener produces quality evidence (coverage, mutation, complexity,
  duplication) and fixes what fails the bars, then forwards to qa.
- qa runs the acceptance and unit suites and verifies the slice against
  its specification, then sends the completion git_handoff to
  specifier,coder,cleaner,architect,hardener. That broadcast is TERMINAL:
  each recipient merges it and stops.
